, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "228535445", "author": {"steamid": "76561198075648709", "personaname": "Gay Lord", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/LordGay/", "num_games_owned": 4439, "num_reviews": 245, "playtime_forever": 1231, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1231, "last_played": 1782089131, "avatar": "e05956206fe40c3c8d15506e2fc5e37b127fbe79"}, "language": "english", "review": "I'm not a Warhammer guy, barely played any of the games as none of them seemed too interesting to me. Played this because a friend got me Space Marine 2 and the story of the second game assumes you know what happened in this game. \n\nIt's a good length (around 7ish hours), good story, super cool enemy designs. The BIGGEST element of the game is definitely the combat, though! It's SUPER fun and brutal, NEVER feels repetitive or boring. Melee mixed with third person shooting is so satisfying! \n\nI did have a couple thing I didn't like. The difficulty seems to ramp up a lot near the end. Like, a massive spike. It turns from power fantasy to cover shooter and makes melee kinda pointless. (And melee is my favorite part of the game :( ) Thankfully, there is A LOT of checkpoints! \n\nThe other is that, while doing executions, you aren't immune to damage. So, if you don't properly time your executions, you can be stuck in an animation while getting absolutely wailed on by other enemies. \n\nAll-in-all, great game. Highly recommend!", "timestamp_created": 1782090601, "timestamp_updated": 1783202610, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 10, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.660827398300170898", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "hardware": {"system